---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RetreatSubNav from '../../../components/RetreatSubNav.astro';
import { AUTHOR_URL, RETREAT_URL } from '../../../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ian, Ros & Milly — Your Hosts"
  description="Meet Ian Johnson and Rosalyn Spencer, your hosts at Longthwaite Writers' Retreat in Cumbria — and Milly, their cockerpoo."
  section="retreat"
>
  <RetreatSubNav current="structured" />

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-8 items-start mb-10">
      <img
        src="/images/ian-and-ros.jpg"
        alt="Ian Johnson and Rosalyn Spencer"
        class="w-full sm:w-56 shrink-0 rounded-2xl shadow-md object-cover"
      />
      <div>
        <span class="font-sans text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-forest">Your Hosts</span>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold text-ink mt-2 mb-4">Ian Johnson &amp; Rosalyn Spencer</h1>
        <p class="font-serif italic text-lg text-ink-light leading-relaxed">
          We are delighted to welcome fellow writers into our home to share a nurturing, creative environment in
          beautiful and peaceful surroundings.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="font-sans text-ink-light leading-relaxed space-y-5 mb-12">
      <p>
        We met in 2001 and were married in Windermere in 2011. We lived in Lincolnshire for many years before one
        of our regular trips to the Lake District in 2021 led to an impromptu decision to sell up and move to
        Cumbria. Since buying our 300-year-old farmhouse near Wigton (just outside the Lake District National
        Park), we&rsquo;ve spent a great deal of our time lovingly renovating the property and redesigning the
        garden, making it a great place for fellow writers to enjoy &mdash; somewhere they can find inspiration
        and be creative.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink pt-4">Rosalyn</h2>
      <p>
        I have been writing for many years as well as holding down full-time positions in teaching and the Youth
        Offending Service. After working part-time for eight years as an Elective Home Education Advisor for a
        local authority, I decided to leave that role to spend more time on my own writing and to run a Writers&rsquo;
        Retreat from our home.
      </p>
      <p>
        My writing is mainly narrative non-fiction promoting a more human-scale approach to education. I have also
        written about parenting, the environment, and a few other issues. I&rsquo;ve had over twenty feature
        articles published in national magazines including Nursery World, The Green Parent, Natural Parent,
        Practical Caravan, and The New Writer. I was also commissioned by a national charity to write a 49-page
        report entitled &lsquo;15 Small Schools&rsquo; based on research I completed for my Master&rsquo;s Degree.
        My first book, &lsquo;Why I Started a Small School&rsquo;, was published in 2014. I am currently working on
        a series of three books &mdash; and hoping the first of these will be published very soon.
      </p>
      <p>
        More information about my writing is available on my <a href={`${AUTHOR_URL}/`} class="text-forest hover:text-forest-dark underline decoration-forest/40 transition-colors">author website</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink pt-4">Ian</h2>
      <p>
        Ian used to be the IT Manager of a graphic design company but retired early due to ill health. He is an
        active member of the Scalefour Model Railway Society &mdash; regularly attending meetings, and working on
        his own model railway layout. Even though Ian says he is no writer, he has written several excellent blogs
        connected to his hobbies and has had articles published in Model Railway magazines.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ian has a passion for cooking and trying out new recipes. Our home frequently has an aroma of freshly made
        bread or some other delicious offering. We grow our own fruit and veg, which we use when we can. The
        cooking for the retreat will be plant-based. Earlier guests have said they had no idea vegan food could be
        so varied and so delicious as they&rsquo;ve sampled his home-made meals, biscuits and cakes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both Ian and myself have Level 2 Awards for Food Safety for Catering. We had our Food Safety Inspection on
        16th June, 2025, and achieved a level 5 (Very Good) Food Hygiene Rating.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink pt-4">Milly</h2>
      <p>
        The final member of our immediate family is our adopted cockerpoo. She&rsquo;s been with us for just over a
        year after her original owners had both sadly died. Milly is extremely friendly and very lovable. She loves
        meeting new house guests &mdash; especially if they tickle her tummy!
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4 border-t border-warm-200">
      <a href={`${RETREAT_URL}/contact`} class="inline-block bg-forest text-white font-sans text-sm font-medium tracking-wide px-7 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-forest-light transition-colors">
        Get in Touch
      </a>
      <a href={`${RETREAT_URL}/structured/apply`} class="inline-block border border-warm-200 text-ink-light font-sans text-sm font-medium tracking-wide px-7 py-3 rounded-full hover:border-forest hover:text-forest transition-colors">
        Application Form
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
